# Extension UID Format

When generating or editing the `uid` field in any `shopify.extension.toml` file, always use a properly formatted UUID v4 string in standard `8-4-4-4-12` hexadecimal format — exactly 36 characters including hyphens (32 hex digits + 4 hyphens).

## Valid example

```text
f1971c5b-3b8a-4c12-84ef-46b88e2ff145
```

## Segment lengths (exact)

| Segment | Length |
|---|---|
| 1 | 8 hex characters |
| 2 | 4 hex characters |
| 3 | 4 hex characters |
| 4 | 4 hex characters |
| 5 | 12 hex characters |

## Rules

- Generate a fresh UUID with `node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomUUID())"` (or equivalent).
- Never truncate, duplicate, concatenate, or pad any segment.
- Never keep scaffolded/malformed uids that are longer or shorter than 36 characters.
- Before saving, verify: total length is 36, and split-by-`-` lengths are `8,4,4,4,12`.
